  "text": "Oncology Care at Salmon Brook Veterinary Hospital\nSkip to content\nKeyboard Accessible Menu\nPlease Call\n(860) 653-7238\n136 Salmon Brook Street,\nGranby, CT 06035\nEquine Pet Portal\nOnline Ordering\nSmall Animal Pet Portal\nHome\nCanine / Feline\nCanine Health Care\nPuppy Care\nSenior Dog Care\nNutrition & Diet\nMicrochipping\nObedience Training\nParasite Protection\nPet Loss\nPet Hospice\nVaccinations\nFeline Health Care\nKitten Care\nSenior Cat Care\nMicrochipping\nNutrition & Diet\nParasite Protection-Cats\nPet Loss\nVaccinations-Cats\nSmall Animal Hospice\nDental Care\nDiagnostic Services\nEmergency Care\nIn-House & Online Pharmacy\nOncology\nSurgery\nPet Loss\nExotic Pet Care\nChicken and Duck Veterinary Care\nPocket Pets/Small Mammals\nReptile Veterinary Care\nExotic Pet Emergency\nBee Medicine\nAbout\nFear Free Care\nJohn B. Violette, DVM\nPaul M. Groshek, DVM, DABVP\nAnne T. Creden, DVM\nChristopher J. Weber, DVM\nAnna B. Wolfe, DVM\nSamantha M. McNamara, DVM\nMonique Fitzpatrick, DVM\nJessica Kaleta, VMD\nRachel Prestigiacomo, DVM\nDelaney Patterson, DVM\nOur Staff\nEquine / Bovine\nEquine Care\nBovine Care\nSmall Ruminant Health Care\nForms\nContact\nEmergency Locations\nOnline Reviews\nPay Bill\nApply for CareCredit\nHome\nCanine / Feline\nCanine Health Care\nPuppy Care\nSenior Dog Care\nNutrition & Diet\nMicrochipping\nObedience Training\nParasite Protection\nPet Loss\nPet Hospice\nVaccinations\nFeline Health Care\nKitten Care\nSenior Cat Care\nMicrochipping\nNutrition & Diet\nParasite Protection-Cats\nPet Loss\nVaccinations-Cats\nSmall Animal Hospice\nDental Care\nDiagnostic Services\nEmergency Care\nIn-House & Online Pharmacy\nOncology\nSurgery\nPet Loss\nExotic Pet Care\nChicken and Duck Veterinary Care\nPocket Pets/Small Mammals\nReptile Veterinary Care\nExotic Pet Emergency\nBee Medicine\nAbout\nFear Free Care\nJohn B. Violette, DVM\nPaul M. Groshek, DVM, DABVP\nAnne T. Creden, DVM\nChristopher J. Weber, DVM\nAnna B. Wolfe, DVM\nSamantha M. McNamara, DVM\nMonique Fitzpatrick, DVM\nJessica Kaleta, VMD\nRachel Prestigiacomo, DVM\nDelaney Patterson, DVM\nOur Staff\nEquine / Bovine\nEquine Care\nBovine Care\nSmall Ruminant Health Care\nForms\nContact\nEmergency Locations\nOnline Reviews\nPay Bill\nApply for CareCredit\nOncology\nHome\n»\nSmall Animal Care\n»\nOncology\nWe Treat Cancer in Pets\nFacing Pet Cancer: Embracing Hope Amidst the Diagnosis\nWe understand that a diagnosis of cancer in your pet can be devastating news, but there is hope. Our staff will be with you and your pet from the very beginning to provide a personalized treatment plan. Using blood tests, x-rays, ultrasounds, and biopsies we will evaluate your pet’s individual case and discuss the best treatment options.\nWe treat cancer in pets with many of the same therapies and drugs that prove successful in treating cancer in humans. Unlike humans, pets often do not experience the same negative side effects from cancer treatment, such as hair loss and nausea. Most pets remain happy and upbeat throughout the entire duration of the treatment.\nWe will discuss the advantages, disadvantages, and potential side effect of each option. Most importantly, we will discuss the quality of life of your pet when discussing the different treatment options with you. We will answer all of your questions and help you keep your family pet as healthy as possible for as long as possible.\nSalmon Brook Veterinary Hospital\n136 Salmon Brook Street\nGranby\n,\nCT\n06035\n860-653-7238\nSalmon Brook Veterinary Hospital is a Veterinary Hospital for all your animals needs in Granby, CT\nhttps://salmonbrookvets.com/\nHours\nM-F – 7:30am – 8:00pm\nSat – 8:00am – 5:00pm\nSun – CLOSED\nAnimal Hospital Affiliations\nAVMA\nAAHA\nCat Friendly Practice®\nCVMA\nAmerican Association of Equine Practitioners\nAmerican Association of Bovine Practitioners\nAmerican Association of Small Ruminant Practitioners\nHospital Policies\nWeb Accessibility Policy\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms of Use\nCareCredit\nApply for CareCredit",
